# Volunteer's Folly

The tendency to volunteer time for causes while ignoring the opportunity cost. People donate hours to organizations without considering what they could have done with that time instead.

## Key Points
- Volunteering feels virtuous but may have high opportunity costs
- Connects to [[opportunity-cost]] thinking
- Connects to [[sunk-cost-fallacy]] — continuing due to past investment
- Connects to [[search-satisficing]] — stopping search prematurely

## Guardrail
Before volunteering, estimate the value of your time and compare it to what you could accomplish elsewhere. This doesn't mean don't volunteer — it means be intentional.
